<span id="A2.p1.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The left side of the first image shows 3 grids, where each grid square is colored with one of 10 possible colors: black, blue, red, green, yellow, gray, magenta, orange, cyan or brown.
The right side of the first image also contains 3 grids, each of which is a transformed version of the corresponding grid on the left. There is a single rule that describes these 3 transformations.</span></span>
